.TH LOOMD 1 "October 2026" "loom 0.9.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
loomd \- Loom background daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loomd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B loomd
is the background daemon that aggregates the Loom subsystem crates
(skills, MCP, sessions, auth, hooks, workflow, routing, knowledge,
telemetry, memory, ACP dispatch, runtimes) and exposes them so the
.BR loom (1)
CLI and other clients can talk to a single long\-lived process
instead of paying startup cost on every invocation.
.PP
It serves three interfaces:
.TP
.B Unix domain socket IPC
A JSON\-line protocol on
.IR LOOM_AGENTS_DIR /loomd.sock
(default
.BR ~/.loom/loomd.sock ).
Unix sockets only \(em there is no TCP or named\-pipe fallback, which
is why native Windows is unsupported and WSL2 is required there.
.TP
.B gRPC server
Listens on
.B 127.0.0.1:50051
by default (override with
.BR LOOM_GRPC_ADDR );
optional TLS via
.B LOOM_GRPC_TLS
with
.B LOOM_GRPC_CERT
and
.BR LOOM_GRPC_KEY .
.TP
.B ZeroMQ event bus
When built with the
.B cross\-process
feature, publishes ecosystem events on
.BR ipc://~/.loom/.loom-events .
.PP
The daemon reads its configuration from
.B ~/.loom/config.toml
(plus any layer overlays under
.BR ~/.loom/config/ ),
stores per\-crate state in
.BR ~/.loom/ ,
and tracks ACP dispatch runs under
.BR ~/.loom/runs/ .
It is normally auto\-started on demand by the
.B loom
CLI, which spawns it with
.B LOOM_AGENTS_DIR
set and records its pid in
.BR ~/.loom/.cache/loomd.pid .
If the daemon receives no IPC traffic for
.B DAEMON_DEFAULT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS
(5 minutes by default), it shuts itself down.
.SH OPTIONS
The daemon takes no command line options; it reads its data
directory from the
.B LOOM_AGENTS_DIR
environment variable (default
.BR .loom )
and its configuration from
.BR ~/.loom/config.toml .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LOOM_AGENTS_DIR
The Loom data directory the daemon operates on (default
.BR .loom ,
relative to the working directory; the CLI passes
.B ~/.loom
when spawning it).
.TP
.B LOOM_GRPC_ADDR
Listen address for the gRPC server (default
.BR 127.0.0.1:50051 ).
.TP
.B LOOM_GRPC_TLS
Set to any value to enable TLS on the gRPC server.
.TP
.B LOOM_GRPC_CERT ", " LOOM_GRPC_KEY
Paths to the TLS certificate and key.
.TP
.B LOOM_DIR
The host Loom data directory mounted read\-only into container
runtimes (docker/podman/kubernetes) so containerized agents can see
the ecosystem.
.TP
.B LOOM_NO_EXTEND ", " LOOM_NO_REMOTE
Set to
.B 1
to skip the
.B extends
or cached\-remote config layer when the daemon loads its
configuration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.loom/config.toml
Main configuration.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/config/
Optional per\-subsystem configuration overlays
(\fBrouting.toml\fR, \fBmcp.toml\fR, \fBhooks.toml\fR, \fBacp.toml\fR).
.TP
.B ~/.loom/loomd.sock
The Unix domain socket the daemon listens on.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/.loom-events
The ZeroMQ socket used to broadcast cross\-process events
(cross\-process feature).
.TP
.B ~/.loom/runs/
ACP dispatch run tracking.
.TP
.BR ~/.loom/.cache/ " (or \fB$CACHE_DIR\fR)"
Snapshot cache used to keep cold starts below the 50ms budget, plus
.B loomd.pid
and the remote config cache
.BR remote_config/ .
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Initiate graceful shutdown: stop accepting new connections, drain
in\-flight requests, then exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown after a
.BR SIGINT / SIGTERM ,
or after the idle timeout fires.
.TP
.B non\-zero
Startup error (could not bind the socket, configuration could not be
parsed, etc.).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR loom (1)
.PP
Project home: <https://github.com/tusharmewara/loom>
